{
  "description": "Languages of the Supertext AI file translation API v1, from GET features on the live API (October 2026). Source codes are bare languages, target codes are what Supertext expects exactly: regional for German, English, French, Italian and Portuguese (de-CH, en-US, pt-BR), a script for Chinese and Serbian (zh-Hans, sr-Latn), a dialect for Swiss German (gsw-u-sd-chzh), bare for the others (es, nl, sl). An integration maps its CMS languages to these codes (a combo box per language, the suggested code preselected); a language nobody mapped gets a default where one is obvious, anything else is an error. 'match': a CMS code that equals a supported code apart from case, '_' for '-' and surrounding spaces gives that code; anything else gives null. 'defaultTargets': the default target for a bare language that Supertext offers only with a region or script: de-DE, en-US, fr-FR, it-IT and pt-PT (the language's home country), zh-Hans (simplified, the most used script) and sr-Latn (as decided for the plugins). Swiss German gets no default: Supertext offers two dialects (gsw-u-sd-chzh, gsw-u-sd-chbe) and neither is the obvious one; no other bare language lacks a bare target. 'defaultTarget': the default for a CMS code without an exact match, compared like 'match': (1) a bare language: its 'defaultTargets' entry, else null; (2) Chinese with a region: zh-TW, zh-HK, zh-MO give zh-Hant, zh-CN, zh-SG give zh-Hans, other regions null; (3) language-Script-REGION whose language-Script is a target gives that target (zh-Hant-TW → zh-Hant, sr-Latn-RS → sr-Latn); (4) language-REGION (two letters or three digits) whose bare language is a target gives the bare target (es-ES, es-419 → es, nl_NL → nl, nb-NO → nb); (5) anything else null: a region of a language Supertext offers only regionally that isn't in the list (de-LI, en-IE, fr-BE, pt-AO, sr-RS, gsw-CH) gets no default, a region is never guessed; codes with more parts (de_DE_formal) need a mapping. A code with an exact match has no default (null). 'suggestTarget': the exact match, else the default, else null (what a settings screen preselects). 'matchSource': exact match as for targets; else, if the code's first subtag (before '-' or '_') is a supported source, that source (source codes have no regions, so en-US as a source is en); else null. 'resolve': the code to send for a CMS code and the integration's mapping (keys compared like 'match'; a non-blank value is sent trimmed and otherwise unchanged, even if it isn't in the list, so a language Supertext adds later can be used before the SDK knows it); for targets: the mapping, else the exact match, else the default, else the error unsupported_language (nothing is sent). For the source, a mapped value is turned into its source form with matchSource (so one mapping serves both directions: {\"de\":\"de-CH\"} sends source de, target de-CH); a mapped value matchSource doesn't know is sent as it is; no mapping: matchSource, else unsupported_language. An empty source stays empty (auto-detect). 'targetOptions': the targets sorted by English name (ordinal comparison), for the combo box; integrations show the name localized where the platform can (Intl.DisplayNames, Locale.getDisplayName, CultureInfo, Babel, Symfony Intl) and the code next to it. 'politeness': whether the target supports politeness more/less; the API answers HTTP 400 FEATURE_ERROR (unsupported_feature) otherwise. Integrations hide the formal/informal choice for those targets; the SDK sends what it is given.",
